Poppler pdftoppm helper (mere aggregation)
=========================================

Penglai ships a target-specific pdftoppm executable and its load-time
dynamic-library closure as a sibling helper next to the product binary.
The helper is spawned as a separate process. It is not linked or dlopened
into Electron or DeepSeek Harness.

Poppler 26.09.0 is GPL-2.0-only OR GPL-3.0-only. Official COPYING (GPLv2)
and COPYING3 (GPLv3) travel next to pdftoppm.

poppler-data 0.4.12 (CJK CMaps and encoding tables) is BSD-3-Clause AND
(GPL-2.0-only OR GPL-3.0-only). Its COPYING, COPYING.adobe, and
COPYING.gpl2 files live under share/poppler.

The macOS 26.09.0 Splash pdftoppm closure includes LGPL libraries
(glib, graphite2, libintl, libiconv) because libpoppler 26.09.0 links
harfbuzz. Those libraries remain part of the spawned helper, not the
Penglai/Electron process.

Windows pdftoppm additionally loads conda-forge libcurl, which PE-imports
libssh2 (OpenSSL libcrypto) and libpsl (icuuc/icudt). Those DLLs are
required load-time closure, not unused ICU.

Do not use Homebrew Poppler bottles or the oschwartz poppler-windows zip
as a Penglai pin.
